WEBVTT

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:10.250
It's the picture.

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:15.160
Mr. Matsuoka!

00:00:18.830 --> 00:00:20.950
Inami Nahoshi, answer me!

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:22.870
Where is Kazuta Haruka?

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:27.830
Awfully compliant of you
to produce this evidence.

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:32.870
Hondomachi!

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:42.660
The second floor!

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:56.500
Stay right where you are.

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:57.540
This is Hondomachi.

00:00:57.540 --> 00:00:58.830
Gravedigger located.

00:00:58.830 --> 00:01:00.080
Two suspects.

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:04.160
The perpetrator Kazuta Haruka and
the mastermind who was directing Kazuta.

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:05.870
Her name is Inami Nahoshi.

00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:07.950
Attempt to arrest met with resistance.

00:01:07.950 --> 00:01:09.450
Mr. Matsuoka was injured.

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:12.200
Kazuta remains armed and continues to resist.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:13.950
Requesting immediate backup!

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:46.950
What is it?

00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:49.410
You have an interesting face.

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:50.830
Do I?

00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:53.700
I haven't seen my face.

00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:56.120
There are no mirrors here.

00:02:57.290 --> 00:02:58.950
True.

00:02:58.950 --> 00:03:02.540
I'm being made to look other than myself.

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:05.830
He says it's to protect
me from the scary monster.

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:07.200
Oh?

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:08.580
Excuse me.

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:12.700
Excuse me. Could you come here?

00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:17.830
Do you think Kazuta ran?

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:19.540
He would never.

00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:22.620
Everything he does is for his princess here.

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:25.080
And isn't she just cool as a cucumber.

00:03:25.080 --> 00:03:27.870
Well, she <i>is </i>an ice queen
who enjoys getting a man

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:30.660
who's not even her boyfriend to kill for her.

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:32.500
Mr. Matsuoka, just shoot her.

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:33.450
Excuse me?

00:03:33.450 --> 00:03:34.750
Please shoot her.

00:03:34.750 --> 00:03:37.000
She's a worthless woman.

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:42.580
If you won't...

00:03:42.580 --> 00:03:44.330
...<i>I </i>will.

00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:21.750
Kazuta!

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:51.410
Cognition particles. Nice.

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:09.450
So what's your deal?

00:05:09.450 --> 00:05:11.950
I wouldn't call it having pride.

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:16.370
True.

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:18.660
It's just being childish.

00:05:22.540 --> 00:05:25.000
Isn't he asking for you?

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:27.000
It's fine. Just ignore him.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:29.160
Do you know how that stuff works?

00:05:30.200 --> 00:05:32.830
Is there someone you have a crush on?

00:05:42.950 --> 00:05:46.040
Uh, sorry, man. Want me to get her?

00:05:46.040 --> 00:05:48.370
Oh, don't worry about it.

00:05:48.370 --> 00:05:50.450
Thank you.

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:53.950
She should still hear me, so it's all right.

00:05:53.950 --> 00:05:56.080
"It's all right"?

00:05:56.080 --> 00:05:57.160
You sure?

00:05:57.160 --> 00:05:58.370
Yes.

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:03.410
Well, if you say so.

00:06:04.830 --> 00:06:07.370
Shall I extract Sakaido?

00:06:07.370 --> 00:06:08.700
Yeah.

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:09.950
Please do.

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:19.290
How many serial killers' wells
have manifested John Walker...

00:06:19.290 --> 00:06:22.290
Kazuta makes six, doesn't he.

00:06:22.290 --> 00:06:25.700
Any connection between him
and the other five serial killers?

00:06:25.700 --> 00:06:28.660
I've run countless queries
with different conditions,

00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:30.660
but so far nothing comes up.

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:33.660
Putting aside how he finds them,

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:36.200
how does he make them into murderers?

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:41.250
To say he controls people's
emotions seems right out of fiction,

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:43.700
but could he be a psychiatrist?

00:06:43.700 --> 00:06:46.120
All six have no treatment records.

00:06:46.120 --> 00:06:49.450
To begin with, he's ingrained
not just in their memories,

00:06:49.450 --> 00:06:51.700
but even in their unconscious!

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:56.120
To dress that way even when he
meets them face to face-- who does that?

00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:57.700
What, is it a cosplay?

00:06:57.700 --> 00:06:59.000
I see.

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:01.580
You're saying that despite how
strange the unconscious can be,

00:07:01.580 --> 00:07:04.250
the fact that all six share the same image of him

00:07:04.250 --> 00:07:09.000
must mean they've actually
seen a man in a red frock coat.

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:10.000
Exactly.

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:13.200
Moreover, that cosplay
bastard produces no witnesses.

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:15.870
He appears only before the person he targets.

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:17.580
It's a nearly impossible feat.

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:19.750
No, I'd say completely impossible.

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:21.700
Hey, you know...

00:07:21.700 --> 00:07:26.290
What if John Walker has a machine
that's similar to the Mizuhanome?

00:07:26.290 --> 00:07:30.000
Except instead of exploring data like the id well,

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:32.830
it can invade a person's unconscious directly.

00:07:32.830 --> 00:07:36.500
Couldn't he be using that to dive in as a pilot?

00:07:37.580 --> 00:07:42.330
There could easily be a second
Mizuhanome, or possibly an original, right?

00:07:42.330 --> 00:07:44.660
After all, we operate the Mizuhanome,

00:07:44.660 --> 00:07:49.540
and even we haven't been given all the details on it.

00:07:49.540 --> 00:07:55.250
Assistant Director Togo, isn't the
Mizuhanome's inventor, Shirakoma Nishio, missing?

00:07:55.250 --> 00:07:56.370
Yes.

00:07:56.370 --> 00:08:00.290
Thanks to that, no one can even access the main unit's central component.

00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:04.080
Can't we get them to
disclose a bit more information?

00:08:04.080 --> 00:08:06.700
I'll try sounding out Chief Hayaseura about it.

00:08:06.700 --> 00:08:10.120
He says it's to prevent military applications,

00:08:10.120 --> 00:08:12.540
and political pressures are a large factor,

00:08:12.540 --> 00:08:15.370
so the info is purposely difficult to dig up.

00:08:15.370 --> 00:08:17.910
Don't even try to get your hands on it.

00:08:17.910 --> 00:08:22.620
The punishment is extremely severe if you're caught.

00:08:22.620 --> 00:08:26.700
Still, it would certainly
help to have more information.

00:08:26.700 --> 00:08:28.200
Wait.

00:08:28.200 --> 00:08:34.620
Even without other Mizuhanome units, the one
at the Wellside that we use now might be plenty.

00:08:34.620 --> 00:08:38.410
In other words, someone
might be using it differently...

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:41.200
...from within the Wellside staff.

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:44.080
Don't say stuff that'll make needless waves.

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:45.200
But...

00:08:45.200 --> 00:08:49.200
...then it might explain why he uses a disguise.

00:08:49.200 --> 00:08:53.620
That means one of our colleagues
could be hiding their face from us.

00:08:53.620 --> 00:08:56.950
But the Mizuhanome was introduced a year ago.

00:08:56.950 --> 00:09:02.000
Take Fukuda Tamotsu for instance.
His first kill was at least three years ago.

00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:06.660
With that timeline, it would have to
have been a Mizuhanome prototype.

00:09:06.660 --> 00:09:09.950
A prototype? That's very possible.

00:09:09.950 --> 00:09:12.790
We're working off of too many hypotheticals.

00:09:12.790 --> 00:09:14.620
Then let's back up.

00:09:14.620 --> 00:09:19.410
How is John Walker finding
his serial killer candidates?

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:21.200
About that.

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:26.580
The variation in distance and timing
gives the impression of being random.

00:09:26.580 --> 00:09:30.160
And yet, some of the killers are connected.

00:09:30.160 --> 00:09:35.540
Fukuda the Perforator and Kazuta Haruka,
his victim as well as the Gravedigger.

00:09:35.540 --> 00:09:40.370
Randomly selected killer candidates
just happened to have a connection?

00:09:40.370 --> 00:09:41.580
I don't think so.

00:09:41.580 --> 00:09:44.160
Yeah, that's a good point.

00:09:44.160 --> 00:09:50.200
That means John Walker arrived at
Kazuta from Fukuda by some method.

00:09:50.200 --> 00:09:54.620
Fukuda's only contact with Kazuta
should be when he put the hole in his head,

00:09:54.620 --> 00:09:59.250
so why, did John Walker just happen to be there?

00:09:59.250 --> 00:10:01.660
It's all too convenient...

00:10:14.410 --> 00:10:17.000
They found mics and cameras.

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:20.620
John Walker really was
monitoring Fukuda after all.

00:10:20.620 --> 00:10:22.450
Then do you suppose...

00:10:22.450 --> 00:10:25.080
Assuming Kazuta was also under surveillance,

00:10:25.080 --> 00:10:29.580
John Walker might have
had his eye on Inami as well.

00:10:29.580 --> 00:10:32.120
Got it. I'll be returning soon.

00:10:32.120 --> 00:10:34.500
Have Narihisago get ready.

00:10:35.580 --> 00:10:36.870
Hey there.

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:39.950
Matsuoka.

00:10:39.950 --> 00:10:41.040
Allow me to convey--

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:44.580
Oh, no need for all that when it's just us.

00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:46.830
Did you meet with the families?

00:10:46.830 --> 00:10:50.410
Of course. How is your shoulder, Matsuoka?

00:10:50.410 --> 00:10:52.540
It's not that serious.

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:56.540
But I stopped you to discuss something else.

00:10:56.540 --> 00:10:59.790
Fukuda Tamotsu... Brilliant detective Anaido.

00:10:59.790 --> 00:11:03.330
I hear he's useless once he's in the well.

00:11:03.330 --> 00:11:08.580
The brilliant detective job doesn't
actually require a criminal, correct?

00:11:08.580 --> 00:11:11.540
If just having killed is good enough,

00:11:11.540 --> 00:11:15.870
then I might just be able to point
you to someone with the aptitude.

00:12:16.870 --> 00:12:18.830
Kaeru.

00:12:18.830 --> 00:12:21.830
The moment her name
passed my lips, I remembered.

00:12:21.830 --> 00:12:24.950
I'm the brilliant detective, Sakaido.

00:12:24.950 --> 00:12:28.620
I must solve the mystery of Kaeru's death.

00:12:30.660 --> 00:12:35.750
Apparently the killer walked down the
aisle after being drenched in her blood.

00:12:51.870 --> 00:12:55.540
Nothing but dead people.

00:12:55.540 --> 00:13:01.250
Still, when did they die, and how
long have they been on this train?

00:13:01.250 --> 00:13:03.160
I've identified the train.

00:13:03.160 --> 00:13:08.450
It's the local train for the line Kazuta
and Inami took to attend high school.

00:13:12.830 --> 00:13:14.370
In the crossing.

00:13:14.370 --> 00:13:16.250
The Gravedigger's victims.

00:13:16.250 --> 00:13:20.330
From front to back, Ayase Minami,
Kouda Shiki, Yamashita Toshiki,

00:13:20.330 --> 00:13:24.000
Shiina Kaori, Masuda Kazuyuki, and Mishima Kana.

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:27.290
They're in the order they died.

00:13:27.290 --> 00:13:30.500
According to the documents,
when Inami Nahoshi was 14,

00:13:30.500 --> 00:13:34.790
her mother committed suicide
by jumping in front of a moving train.

00:13:34.790 --> 00:13:40.830
Apparently the train Sakaido is on
is the one that ran her mother over.

00:13:44.370 --> 00:13:49.790
Moreover, Inami Nahoshi was aboard
this very train when it happened.

00:13:49.790 --> 00:13:50.870
Look.

00:14:05.580 --> 00:14:08.370
The last car and the first car connect.

00:14:08.370 --> 00:14:10.620
So the train forms a ring.

00:14:10.620 --> 00:14:17.700
Hello.

00:14:17.700 --> 00:14:20.000
I've been waiting for you.

00:14:22.830 --> 00:14:26.700
You killed Kaeru-- that girl?

00:14:26.700 --> 00:14:29.950
Huh? You mean her?

00:14:35.950 --> 00:14:37.790
She died.

00:14:37.790 --> 00:14:40.540
So you didn't kill her, then?

00:14:40.540 --> 00:14:41.700
What do you think?

00:14:41.700 --> 00:14:43.370
I imagine not.

00:14:43.370 --> 00:14:48.580
Your hands are bloody from that handkerchief,
but there's no sign of blood spatter on you.

00:14:48.580 --> 00:14:54.830
To begin with, the killer would've disposed of
both the handkerchief and those bloody shoes.

00:14:54.830 --> 00:14:58.540
Upon closer inspection, there's
not much blood at the scene.

00:14:58.540 --> 00:15:02.660
And the footsteps could
well be Kaeru's shoe size.

00:15:02.660 --> 00:15:05.000
So her name was Kaeru.

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:05.950
Huh.

00:15:05.950 --> 00:15:09.370
You also didn't know her name.

00:15:09.370 --> 00:15:12.450
Meaning there's no reason
for you to want to kill her.

00:15:14.000 --> 00:15:16.750
Well, not that it really matters.

00:15:26.370 --> 00:15:29.290
Hey, don't look at him.

00:15:29.290 --> 00:15:30.330
Your boyfriend?

00:15:30.330 --> 00:15:32.160
As if.

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:35.080
Okay... Just a few more questions.

00:15:35.080 --> 00:15:38.870
I suppose Kaeru circled
the train covered in blood,

00:15:38.870 --> 00:15:42.870
and then asked you to wipe off her feet?

00:15:42.870 --> 00:15:46.620
Yeah. I don't know why, though.

00:15:46.620 --> 00:15:48.410
<i>I </i>do.

00:15:48.410 --> 00:15:53.450
Kaeru did it to lead me here.

00:15:53.450 --> 00:15:55.950
In order to bring me to this girl.

00:15:55.950 --> 00:16:00.160
Or possibly to bring me to this boy.

00:16:00.160 --> 00:16:05.200
Hey, do you know when this
train reaches the next station?

00:16:05.200 --> 00:16:08.500
My mom's probably waiting for me there.

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:16.790
If her mother's at the next station,
then won't she never be hit by the train?

00:16:16.790 --> 00:16:19.830
Perhaps Inami Nahoshi is protecting her mother?

00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:21.040
No.

00:16:21.040 --> 00:16:23.660
It was at the crossing they passed earlier.

00:16:23.660 --> 00:16:25.790
That's where her mother jumped.

00:16:25.790 --> 00:16:28.410
The time also fits perfectly.

00:16:28.410 --> 00:16:29.290
In other words--

00:16:29.290 --> 00:16:34.290
Inami Nahoshi is forever aboard
the train as it runs over her mother.

00:16:34.290 --> 00:16:35.370
Hey.

00:16:35.370 --> 00:16:36.700
Just now.

00:16:40.000 --> 00:16:42.040
How awful.

00:16:42.040 --> 00:16:46.120
Does this mean Kazuta and Inami
committed murders they otherwise wouldn't

00:16:46.120 --> 00:16:47.620
because of John Walker?

00:16:47.620 --> 00:16:50.120
Impulses don't determine actions.

00:16:50.120 --> 00:16:52.080
How do we know that?

00:16:52.080 --> 00:16:57.200
Isn't that an assumption, like whether humans
are fundamentally good or fundamentally evil?

00:16:57.200 --> 00:16:59.330
Or whether reason holds primacy.

00:16:59.330 --> 00:17:03.330
That human reason must be
strong enough to beat out impulse.

00:17:03.330 --> 00:17:04.790
That idea.

00:17:14.660 --> 00:17:16.580
You sure I'm not interrupting?

00:17:16.580 --> 00:17:19.870
Jeez. I told you to quit it with that.

00:17:23.450 --> 00:17:24.950
I...

00:17:24.950 --> 00:17:28.330
I hate seeing someone dead.

00:17:28.330 --> 00:17:32.580
The incident with her mother
must have warped those feelings.

00:17:32.580 --> 00:17:35.910
Inami Nahoshi revealed the location of a barrel.

00:17:37.000 --> 00:17:39.450
You're being awfully compliant.

00:17:39.450 --> 00:17:42.620
I mean, now that I can't view them by camera,

00:17:42.620 --> 00:17:45.910
there's no point keeping them like that, is there?

00:17:45.910 --> 00:17:49.250
I'll tell you where the rest are
buried, too, just as you want.

00:18:04.370 --> 00:18:06.700
Wanna join us?

00:18:06.700 --> 00:18:08.620
Stop that.

00:18:09.830 --> 00:18:13.160
I want it to be this way forever.

00:18:13.160 --> 00:18:14.330
What do we do?

00:18:14.330 --> 00:18:16.500
They've located all the victims' remains,

00:18:16.500 --> 00:18:18.950
and it seems the case has drawn to a close.

00:18:18.950 --> 00:18:22.910
Let's... let Sakaido do
what he wants a little longer.

00:18:22.910 --> 00:18:25.870
No, I mean, I also...

00:18:25.870 --> 00:18:29.410
I want to go on looking at this world.

00:18:29.410 --> 00:18:31.160
Is that strange?

00:18:47.450 --> 00:18:49.160
Copy that.

00:18:50.500 --> 00:18:52.910
The remains have all been recovered.

00:18:54.910 --> 00:18:56.700
I see.

00:18:58.830 --> 00:19:00.330
Um.

00:19:00.330 --> 00:19:06.410
Could I perhaps meet with Ms. Hondomachi,
that cute detective who arrested me?

00:19:06.410 --> 00:19:07.830
I don't know.

00:19:07.830 --> 00:19:11.000
Is there something you want to tell her?

00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:15.700
Both she and Kazuta have holes in their heads.

00:19:15.700 --> 00:19:21.500
So I just wanted to see
whether they had a connection.

00:19:22.500 --> 00:19:24.700
I don't see what you mean.

00:19:24.700 --> 00:19:27.500
I know <i>she'll </i>understand.

00:19:27.500 --> 00:19:29.750
Because she's a girl.

00:19:29.750 --> 00:19:33.080
What? Me? A brilliant detective?

00:19:33.080 --> 00:19:34.540
Really?

00:19:34.540 --> 00:19:35.370
Yes.

00:19:35.370 --> 00:19:41.450
Mr. Matsuoka made a suggestion with regard
to your preeminent powers of deduction.

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:45.660
Ms. Hondomachi.

00:19:45.660 --> 00:19:46.700
Yes?

00:19:46.700 --> 00:19:52.160
Can I count on your help in the investigation
of serial killer creator John Walker?

00:19:52.160 --> 00:19:53.450
Of course.

00:19:53.450 --> 00:19:58.330
I have great expectations for your performance.

00:19:58.330 --> 00:19:59.910
I'll try to meet them!

00:20:01.290 --> 00:20:03.870
<i>Kaeru killed herself.</i>

00:20:03.870 --> 00:20:06.040
<i>"This train doesn't go anywhere."</i>

00:20:06.040 --> 00:20:08.160
<i>"It just goes around in circles."</i>

00:20:08.160 --> 00:20:10.660
<i>Just to tell me that.</i>

00:20:12.000 --> 00:20:14.790
<i>How could she do such a thing?</i>

00:20:14.790 --> 00:20:21.790
<i>Is Kaeru's death--is anyone's
death worth something like that?</i>

00:20:21.790 --> 00:20:23.700
<i>I just don't understand.</i>

00:20:26.500 --> 00:20:28.870
Where are we?

00:20:32.250 --> 00:20:36.330
Since we'll never arrive anywhere,
I guess it doesn't matter.

00:20:40.830 --> 00:20:43.500
You don't have to die!

00:20:43.500 --> 00:20:46.080
I don't want you to die!

00:20:46.080 --> 00:20:47.500
I...

00:20:48.500 --> 00:20:51.160
I just wanted to save you!

00:20:57.290 --> 00:20:59.120
Mr. Matsuoka!

00:21:00.500 --> 00:21:02.950
Thank you so much for what you did.

00:21:02.950 --> 00:21:05.120
You don't need to thank me.

00:21:06.040 --> 00:21:09.700
Well, I suppose you were just doing your job, but...

00:21:09.700 --> 00:21:13.580
No, I mean it's nothing to feel good about.

00:21:13.580 --> 00:21:17.160
I didn't want to make you a damn detective.

00:21:17.160 --> 00:21:20.620
I wish you didn't have it in you.

00:21:20.620 --> 00:21:24.410
But it means I'll be entrusted
with difficult, important work.

00:21:24.410 --> 00:21:28.040
Do you know what makes a brilliant detective?

00:21:28.040 --> 00:21:30.660
Their powers of deduction, I suppose?

00:21:30.660 --> 00:21:34.950
Right. And there's the prerequisite
for diving into an id well.

00:21:34.950 --> 00:21:37.410
You have to have killed.

00:21:37.410 --> 00:21:40.790
Apparently, to be a brilliant
detective within the well,

00:21:40.790 --> 00:21:43.580
it's also not good enough just to have killed.

00:21:43.580 --> 00:21:46.750
You have to be a serial killer.

00:21:46.750 --> 00:21:51.040
I don't fault you for your attempted suicide
when you were captured by Fukuda.

00:21:51.040 --> 00:21:52.370
But I wonder,

00:21:52.370 --> 00:21:57.160
why did you split at Oono Genpei's house
and go to the basement on your own?

00:21:59.120 --> 00:22:03.870
Just how early on did you realize that
Inami Nahoshi was the Gravedigger?

00:22:03.870 --> 00:22:07.000
Or should I say, when you
sent the picture to the others,

00:22:07.000 --> 00:22:09.660
just how high did you think the probability was?

00:22:09.660 --> 00:22:10.500
I--

00:22:10.500 --> 00:22:14.830
When you used cognition particle detection
as a pretext and killed Kazuta Haruka,

00:22:14.830 --> 00:22:16.870
just how great did it feel?

00:22:22.450 --> 00:22:23.620
That's not...

00:22:23.620 --> 00:22:27.000
It's fine. I'm not condemning you.

00:22:27.000 --> 00:22:29.330
Particularly at this organization,

00:22:29.330 --> 00:22:32.870
I suppose that sort of thing
is compatible with justice.

00:22:32.870 --> 00:22:38.790
All I did by recommending you was
protect myself and my other colleagues.

00:22:47.580 --> 00:22:52.540
Director, about the cameras and microphones
hidden in Fukuda Tamotsu's house.

00:22:52.540 --> 00:22:55.750
They matched items seized in a past case.

00:22:55.750 --> 00:22:57.040
A past case?

00:22:57.040 --> 00:23:00.080
The serial killer called the Challenger.

00:23:00.080 --> 00:23:03.750
The man who murdered Narihisago's daughter. Katsuyama Denshin.

00:23:03.750 --> 00:23:07.500
They're the same as the
equipment found hidden in his home.
